;;; members: assembly optimization escalation
;;; moved into design-decision items: p-retrieval-pipeline-need (escalating layers instead of one-shot retrieval); p-retrieval-tool-choice (choose the tool by the strongest anchor); p-explorer-subagent-search (broad search delegated to an isolated subagent)
;;; children (:include / :frame, in the text's order): decisions (each item one copy of opendev.design-decision.lisp)
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: the caption of Figure 15
(defrule retrieval -> decisions retrieval-assembly retrieval-optimization retrieval-escalation)
(defrule decisions -> :instruction "探索で下した設計の決定を、1 行に 1 つ決定の名前で挙げる。段階的に強める探索、手掛かりからの道具選び、広い探索の委譲のうち、このハーネスにあるもの" :frame "opendev.design-decision.lisp")
(defrule retrieval-assembly -> :nucleus retrieval-assembly/sources :elaboration-process-step retrieval-assembly/validate)
(defrule retrieval-assembly/sources -> :instruction "探した結果以外に、モデルへ渡す材料を、数と順で 1 文で書く" :sample "Before each model call, ContextPicker assembles the final message list from six ordered sources: (1) the system prompt augmented with selected playbook strategies from the adaptive memory (Section 2.3.6), (2) project-level and user-level persistent rules, (3) inline @file references and image blocks supplied by the user, (4) the conversation history retrieved from SessionManager, (5) system reminders injected at the point of decision (Section 2.3.4), and (6) the current user query.")
(defrule retrieval-assembly/validate -> :instruction "組み上げた構造の検証と修復を 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled structure is validated by ValidatedMessageList, which enforces structural integrity (every assistant message with tool calls must be followed by matching tool results before the next user turn) and auto-repairs violations with synthetic error placeholders rather than failing outright.")
(defrule retrieval-optimization -> :instruction "組み上げた文脈が、予算に収まるように通る処理を 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled context passes through ContextCompactor for token-budget enforcement before entering the ReAct reasoning loop.")
(defrule retrieval-escalation -> :instruction "探索の段階が、簡単な問いと複雑な問いで使い分けられることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The four layers form a retrieval pipeline that mirrors the escalation pattern seen in agentic search systems [85]: simple queries resolve at Layer 1 with a single tool call; complex queries escalate to Layer 2’s multi-step search; all results converge at Layer 3’s assembly; and Layer 4 enforces the token budget.")
